R-CH10 R-EC19 (slice 238, Design Q613 item 4): each command that reads both files compares the tables. The `roc` proxy without `+<id>` and without ROC_TOOLCHAIN loads through `Base.load!` with the source `Read` (the only caller of that source), not through `ResolveLoad` as `tln install` does. config.toml has [channels.reify]; the talon.toml of p1 has another source and the one of p2 another tag-prefix: exit 19 `is not equal to`, the compiler does not run. If `channels_equal` of Base.roc is turned off, the proxy goes on (it selects the pin of the header and runs `exec`), so exit, stderr and calls.log differ. The texts are proposals (TW24).
